{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgirEQddDvbPCypxHxevb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Refuter report: Theorem 7.1, its two proofs, Algorithm 7.2 (2026-11-05)\n\nWritten to `/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/07_algorithms/refuter.md`; scratch scripts `refuter_check.py`, `refuter_alg72.py`, `refuter_uncapped.py`, `refuter_n7.py` in the same directory. Nothing else was modified; nothing committed.\n\n## Coverage\n\n- All 209 graphs on ≤ 6 vertices (`graph_atlas_g`); `cw(G)` and `vs(L(G))` exact by subset DP over prefix sets (equivalent to the minimum over permutations). 19 have a single-edge component; 85 are subcubic without one; 4 are stars `K_{1,Δ}`, `Δ = 2..5`.\n- Bonus: 1,025 of the 1,044 graphs on 7 vertices (`m ≤ 16`), inequalities only.\n- Proof (i) map, rule exactly as stated, under **both** labellings of `e_q = uw`: every L-layout for `m ≤ 7` (164,425 layouts × 2), and for `m ≥ 8` every optimal L-layout up to a cap of 20,000 per graph plus 300 random layouts (1,237,872 layouts × 2); 2,804,594 map checks. The cap was hit on 54 of the `m ≥ 8` graphs; the uncapped run (cap 3,000,000) is **not finished**.\n- Proof (ii) map from **every** vertex layout: 115,820 layouts (21,428 optimal).\n- Algorithm 7.2 end to end on all 104 subcubic graphs to 6 vertices: value = exact `cw`, witness attains it, 104 of 104.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **No violation of (i), (ii), `cw ≤ max(1, vs(L))`, or the `Δ ≤ 3` equality** on the 209 graphs to 6 vertices and 1,025 at 7. Star values and the excess `⌊Δ/2⌋ − 1` check at `Δ = 2..5`.\n2. **Proof (i) holds per layout**, optimal or not, under both labellings, on every graph without a single-edge component. The rule is labelling-dependent in which endpoint goes first but both choices satisfy the bound. Editorial: say so in one clause.\n3. **Proof (i), sentence by sentence: no gap.** Claims A and B correct; `deg u = a_u + 1 + b_u` gives the cut identity; the `b_u + b_w` extra edges at L-cut `q − 1` are placed, have an unplaced neighbour, avoid `P`, and are pairwise distinct; arithmetic right; \"both fail\" is exactly `N(u) = {w}`, `N(w) = {u}`; `q = 1` covered.\n4. **Proof (ii), sentence by sentence: no gap.** All arithmetic checks; \"x before `v_i`\" works whether or not `x` is the earlier endpoint; `min(a_i, b_i) ≤ ⌊Δ/2⌋`; `b_i = 0` has no such cut; the later-endpoint tie order is never used (editorial).\n5. **The map of (i) fails on graphs *with* a single-edge component, which the text neither claims nor says** — editorial. Concrete: path `0—1—2` plus `3—4`, L-layout `(0,1), (3,4), (1,2)` has `vs = 1`, mapped order `0, 4, 3, 1, 2` has cutwidth 2. 1,924 such triples; the theorem's inequality `cw ≤ max(1, vs(L))` remains true by components and Algorithm 7.2 sets the edges aside first.\n6. **Algorithm 7.2 correctness: correct as written**; verified with my own pipeline and with the repo's `cutwidth_subcubic`. `O(m²)` for the maps is a safe over-statement.\n7. **First-draft remark** (path `0—4—3—2`): checked by hand, correct — degree-tie order has cutwidth 2, the rule gives cutwidth 1.\n8. **Base table arithmetic**: all values and the cyclomatic-number restatement correct.\n9. **Not checked** (outside the assigned lines): the `G°`-contraction remark and the Kitsunai et al. attributions.\n\n## Code (`learning/subexp_algorithms.py`, read last)\n\n- `vertex_layout_from_line_layout`: the proof's rule exactly, `u` = lower-indexed endpoint, `P` = vertices completed strictly earlier; 0 mismatches against my implementation on all 164,425 L-layouts for `m ≤ 7`.\n- `line_layout_from_vertex_layout`: (earlier position, later position, index) — the proof's order; 0 mismatches on all 115,820 vertex layouts.\n- `cutwidth_subcubic`: Algorithm 7.2 as stated; exact on all 104 subcubic graphs. Docstring nit: \"for `Δ ≥ 4` the returned value is `vs(L(G))`\" is off by the `max(·, 1)` when `G'` is empty and a single edge exists.\n- `vs_layout`: DP witness attains the DP value on every graph tested.\n\nverdict: no wrong statement found"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3667,"cache_read_input_tokens":98526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3667,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":944,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018UMrVdD7PByDwntxq8UTGY","agent_id":"ae9e08a9fa737ce4f","session_id":"09aaa989-9eda-444c-a4fd-1cc6d69ace0c","uuid":"85976a02-d2ff-4e44-9ac0-46792694be90","timestamp":"2026-11-05T00:40:08.698Z","request_id":"req_011CgirEQEZkzdNh6swDqAJi","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Refute §7.1 proofs blind"}
