d run was stopped unfinished by PID and is not","+  cited.","+- `literature/MISSING.md`: Makedon & Sudborough 1989, Chung & Seymour","+  1989, Korach & Solel 1993, Monien & Sudborough 1988, Yannakakis 1985","+  recorded (the owner's note in TASK.md). `.gitignore`: the extracts.","+- Gate: `python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0014/gate.py` **PASS**","+  (`07_algorithms/gate.log`): `lake build` ok (no Lean file changed),","+  0 `sorry`, no `axiom`, tests 1,978 passed / 2 skipped / 1 xfailed","+  (279 s), `pathwidth_solver` 123 passed (398 s), paper check clean. The","+  only change after the gate is a docstring sentence in","+  `cutwidth_subcubic` (the refuter's nit); the item's 10 tests re-run","+  green after it.","+","+### Blockers","+","+None. Not committed (the driver commits). `solutions/` untouched; no run","+on any instance; nothing downloaded; no Lean file changed.","+","+### Next","+","+Item 08 formalises Theorem 7.1 (both directions; the tie rule of (i) is","+what the formal proof must carry, and the single-edge exception is part","+of the statement), Theorem 4.1 and Theorem 4.4 against","+`VertexSeparation.lean`, with a cutwidth definition stated there; §7.1's","+proofs are written to be taken as they stand, and `refuter.md` lists what","+was checked per layout. Item 09 takes §7.4's table as the model of a row","+and should carry Algorithm 7.2's honest base (`1.89^{m/n}`) wherever a","+`Complex/` problem meets cutwidth; item 10 records that the cutwidth open","+problem of Bentert et al. is untouched. Item 11 adds Kitsunai et al.'s","+witness remark and the five `MISSING.md` entries to the note."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/Ralph_Loops/loop0014/iterations.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":122,"oldLines":7,"newStart":122,"newLines":7,"lines":["   least independent set, with the encoding's correctness proved. Brute","   force to 7 vertices for every encoding. Write §6."," ","-- [ ] **07 New exact algorithms by exact linear transformation, unconditional.**","+- [x] **07 New